<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Stability of Main Experimental Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the standard deviation of DELTAformer’s forecasting performance across 3 independent runs, reported in <a href="#A1.T5" title="In A.4 Stability of Main Experimental Results ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ Transformer Modeling for Both Scalability and Performance in Multivariate Time Series" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. We report that DELTAformer’s forecasting accuracy is stable and repeatable across datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T5" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A1.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Forecasting performance and their standard deviations after 3 independent runs.</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
