<figure id="A5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="A5.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Full short-term forecasting results (96 time-steps predicting {12, 24, 48, 96} time-steps): For short-term forecasting benchmark, we utilize 4 versions of well acknowledged PEMS datasets. We follow the experimental setup of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">LIU et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. The average performance across all forecast horizons for each dataset are also reported.</span></figcaption>
